{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1137249-vtm-recruitment-baltimore-by-night","id":1137249,"title":"VtM Recruitment: Baltimore by Night","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-04T02:37:54-07:00","id":1137249,"title":"VtM Recruitment: Baltimore by Night","content":"Exactly what the tin says. I'm recruiting players for a Vampire: The Masquerade game! The game is run through Skype, mostly via real time text sessions, though I will allow voice sessions for whoever is interested. I'm big on narrative, though I let the dice do their job. I generally have a flexible schedule, but I prefer to run sessions in the afternoon or evening, Eastern Standard Time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronicle Blurb</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Borderlands: cHarm City Madhouse</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Mood: Gothic-Noir Thriller<br /> <br /> Themes: Existential Unease, Classism, Civil Breakdown, Addiction<br /> <br /> Setting: Baltimore, Maryland<br /> <br /> Everyone lies. That\u2019s true, and real liars fucking love that. Lies are just a tool, though. Like any good tool, they\u2019re useful. Like many tools, they can be used with malice. The world is full of goddamn tools, and the Kindred of Bodymore know that well. Some of these tools have names and faces. All of these tools can be dangerous. One of these tools might be you.<br /> According to the Prince of Washington DC, Baltimore is a Camarilla domain under their control. If you ask the locals, though, that\u2019s the biggest lie of them all.. Nobody rules Baltimore. Kindred try, forming cults or playing at politics, but since the 60s, the city has been fractured. Some say it\u2019s a sign of social decay, and some blame the corruption filtering in from the political sleaze of the nation\u2019s capital. Many just chalk it up to times changing, shrug, and move on with their night. Maybe they\u2019re all correct, in their own way. The end result is disorder, whatever the cause.<br /> The Camarilla tries to install lesser \u201clords\u201d, as Princes under the sway of DC and Virginia. The Anarchs rally fiery Kindred and try to establish philosophy driven Baronies. They all get knocked down a peg, shown the door, and often shown the dawn as a parting gift. Nobody is holding the keys to the city. Nobody keeps the peace. Nobody lasts long enough to bring order to chaos. Nobody sees the bigger picture, either, and maybe that\u2019s a good thing. If you dig too deeply, you might actually find something.<br /> The city may be in turmoil now, but maybe your coterie can change things. Perhaps hope for stability comes with you. Kindred will seek power, one way or another. Kindred nature abhors a power vacuum. Is Baltimore going to be another casualty in the seemingly endless struggle or become something more? It has to become something. Night by night, the world changes. Night after night, it's always the same. Something has to change. You're the new blood, and this city is open to you, for better or worse. You've got your chance to make your move, whatever it is. The world is in disarray. What are you going to do about it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Playable Sect Affiliations: Anarch, Camarilla, Independent<br /> <br /> Coterie size: 2-4 player characters<br /> <br /> Character age: Neonate, Embraced no earlier than the 1980s<br /> <br /> Playable Clans/Bloodlines: Brujah, Caitiff, Gangrel (City, Standard, Mariner), Followers of Set, Lasombra, Malkavian (Dominate), Nosferatu, Ravnos, Toreador, Tremere, Tzimisce (Anarch Only), Ventrue<br /> <br /> <br /> Ruleset: V20 (with supplemental material from VtDA 20th)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All Merits and Flaws must be cleared with the ST<br /> <br /> <br /> You can contact me via private message here on the forums, email or by simply posting your interest and/or questions below.<br /> <br /> Email: <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#0869727a696d646e617a6d7b7c677a654860677c65696164266b6765\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"4223383023272e242b302731362d302f022a2d362f232b2e6c212d2f\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a><br /> Skype: morningsidekiller1","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 09-04-2017, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T19:17:42-07:00","id":1137897,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your message.<br /> <br /> Yes, I'm still interested in playing as a Camarilla character in your Baltimore setting, and can contact you via Skype this weekend. I apologize for my delayed response, as I realize I said I would create a character last weekend or so. It's taking me a bit of time because this is my first actual time playing the game, and so I'm not certain how much additional detail beyond the technical character sheet should be included -- (e.g. a short 1-2 page written description or summary 